From 7a4f0926b6837d05db6bcce4806ec7888b5847db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: norm wasm <blake@comatri.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:52:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] core: wasm FFI backend and browser build

platform/ffi-wasm.ts adapts an instance of the wasm32-wasi core to the
FfiBackend surface (dlopen/ptr/toArrayBuffer), with a minimal WASI shim
(fd 1/2 to host callbacks, clocks, random, environ; no filesystem).

- selected when globalThis.__OPENTUI_WASM__ is set (browsers instantiate
  first, then import @opentui/core) or OPENTUI_BACKEND=wasm (Bun/Node,
  module from OPENTUI_WASM_PATH, next to the bundle, or the zig output)
- ptr(jsBuffer) stages a copy in linear memory; regions passed directly
  as arguments are copied back after each call (out-parameters) and
  released once the synchronous turn ends
- toArrayBuffer copies; toNativeView (new, all backends) aliases native
  memory and is used for OptimizedBuffer planes and NativeSpanFeed
- callbacks are re-exported from tiny generated modules and installed in
  the core's function table (made growable at load time)
- u32/ptr/bool/u64 returns normalized to Bun's conventions
- bun-ffi-structs is pointed at the backend (4-byte pointers) through
  globalThis.__BUN_FFI_STRUCTS_BACKEND__ (needs the matching
  bun-ffi-structs patch)
- #opentui/runtime-assets gains a browser variant; the lib build adds
  index.browser.js (exports "." browser condition), wasm.js
  (@opentui/core/wasm) and ships opentui.wasm
